Chapter: Tuple

 Anonymous product types. `(a, b)` is sugar for `Tup2 a b`, `(a, b, c)`
 for `Tup3 a b c`, and so on up to five. Build one with the tuple
 expression `(x, y)`; take it apart with a tuple pattern in `when`:
 `is (x, y) -> ...`. Each `TupN` is a single-constructor variant, so a
 tuple pattern is always exhaustive.

Section: Definitions

  Tup2 (a) (b) =
    | MkTup2 (a) (b)

  Tup3 (a) (b) (c) =
    | MkTup3 (a) (b) (c)

  Tup4 (a) (b) (c) (d) =
    | MkTup4 (a) (b) (c) (d)

  Tup5 (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) =
    | MkTup5 (a) (b) (c) (d) (e)

  pair-first : (a, b) -> a
  pair-first (p) =
   let (x, y) = p in x

  pair-second : (a, b) -> b
  pair-second (p) =
   let (x, y) = p in y

